  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rohingya Response and National Resilience Programme (RRNRP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Rohingya Response and National Resilience Programme (RRNRP), led by NRC with consortium partners HI, IRC, and DRC, aims to strengthen protection, health, education, and advocacy services for Rohingya refugees and host communities in Cox&#x2019;s Bazar. The project enhances access to essential health care, inclusive education, legal and protection services, and promotes disability inclusion across humanitarian interventions. HI&#x2019;s role focuses on delivering comprehensive rehabilitation, MHPSS and protection support for persons with disabilities, elderly persons, and individuals with injuries or impairments in seven camps and Hnila Union. HI also leads on disability-inclusive advocacy through developing technical tools and training modules under the Age and Disability Technical Working Group (ADTWG). Additionally, HI contributes to ensuring inclusive approaches across consortium interventions and coordination platforms.</narrative>
  </description>
